Subject: [PATCH 3/5] feat(catalog): tenant-scoped admin lead capture service

captureLead / listLeads / moveLead over the EXISTING createLeadSchema contract,
Lead/LeadStage/canMoveLead domain and the leads table (migration 0000).
No schema, migration, auth, routing or with-tenant change.

- Strict, normalising refinement of createLeadSchema: client-supplied tenantId,
  stage, id or createdAt are rejected; name/message trimmed; phone stored as
  digits with optional '+'.
- Every query runs in withTenant under nile_app, so isolation is enforced by
  RLS; another tenant's lead is indistinguishable from a missing one.
- moveLead follows canMoveLead and updates conditionally on the stage read.
- Errors are DomainError codes (validation_failed, lead_not_found,
  invalid_lead_transition, lead_stage_conflict) so apps/api toHttp maps them.

19 PGlite tests: valid capture, 13 invalid inputs, RLS isolation (list,
no-context, WITH CHECK 42501, cross-tenant move), filters, transitions.
Not wired to apps/api: routing is shared with the POS/payments work.
